From 106077933fdbfbc712135e6df3d27c3db3735aed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReArc Overlay <overlay@rearc.invalid>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 01:54:06 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 wave 32: embedded video Picture-in-Picture and
 media actions for the host

Arc renders its PiP video into a native view the shell places, not a
floating Chromium window. With ReArcEngineSetVideoOverlayCallback set,
ChromeContentBrowserClient::CreateWindowForVideoPictureInPicture returns a
HostVideoOverlay for a tab that entered PiP through the bridge: a
content::VideoOverlayWindow that owns a layer-hosting NSView, a
RecyclableCompositorMac and a DisplayCALayerTree, and shows the video's
surface (AddChildFrameSink + LayerSurface) aspect-fit in black. The video
keeps its native frame rate while the tab is hidden, and the compositor
draws only while a session is shown and the view is in a window. Events:
created (+1 view), shown, hidden, closed, natural size, coalesced and
deduplicated state, position, source title, first CALayer update. Calls:
ReArcVideoOverlayAction (transport, mute, back to tab, close), Seek,
SetBounds (sizes the renderer's video) and ReadPixel (a CopyOutputRequest
read-back of the composited view). Without the callback tab/048's window is
unchanged. ReArcTabGetMediaActions publishes the media session's actions as
bits, and a media event now follows every change of them. ABI 1.43 /
bridge 0.45.0 (pip_embedded); framework.exports and framework.order list
the six new functions. Existing ABI layouts remain unchanged.

Last rebased: 2026-11-05 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.74 (d331de35ca).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
